# slop-lint waivers for Michael's Corner.
# Format: path/suffix: rule,rule   (or `*` for every rule)
# Scoped per rule on purpose. These files are still linted for everything else.
#
# Two files exist to CATALOGUE banned vocabulary. They cannot do their job
# without containing the words the copy rules forbid.

# The AI-slop detector tool. Its buzzword list IS the product.
tools/ai-slop-detector.html: slop-copy,em-dash

# The "remove AI flavor" prompt. It names the phrases the model must hunt down,
# and the text is copied verbatim by the reader, so a token cannot be injected.
prompts/remove-ai-flavor.html: slop-copy

# Planning docs that quote the forbidden patterns inside their own prohibitions
# ("no 'Most Popular' badge", "no 'trusted by' strips"), and the spec for the
# slop detector, which has to enumerate the vocabulary it catches. Not shipped.
planning/DIRECTION.md: slop-copy,most-popular-badge,trusted-by,not-just-but
planning/PERSONA-solo.md: trusted-by,slop-copy
planning/CONTENT-LIBRARY.md: slop-copy
planning/TOOLS.md: slop-copy
